          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Designated Leader" id="9795-89e7-8c28-e5ba" hidden="false" targetId="1f95-fa4a-51e0-80f8" type="rule"/>
            <infoLink name="Hero Actions" id="60cc-9b60-482b-9604" hidden="false" targetId="ca2a-7f10-72a9-2a56" type="profile"/>
            <infoLink name="Formation (Specified)" id="98f2-05c4-0677-3ebc" hidden="false" targetId="5ffd-5449-427f-b767" type="rule">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="name" type="append" value="Corporate Mercenaries"/>
                <modifier field="description" type="append" value="Corporate Mercenaries"/>
              </modifiers>
            </infoLink>
          </infoLinks>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Leverage Your Assets" id="a6a6-be01-6bb2-1b3f" hidden="false">
              <description>Each time this Unit uses the Private Military Contractors Special Rule to perform an Action, instead of spending the resources to do so, record the cost, this is now Debt, then continue as normal. 


* Interest Due: At the beginning of the next Command Phase, roll an X+ Check where X is equal to Debt you have accrued. Add or subtract an amount of SP to your Debt equal to the amount this Check was failed or succeeded by. 


* Shifting Loyalties: At the start of the Command Phase, you may choose to pay your Debt. If you fail to fully pay your Debt, your Opponent may choose to cover the amount you owe. If they do, they immediately gain control of this Unit. If both Players decline to cover the debt, this Unit immediately Activates. Once Activated, it must perform an Attack Action targeting the nearest friendly Unit, and then an Attack Action targeting the nearest Enemy Unit.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="You Don&apos;t Don&apos;t Pay Enough For Me To Lead" id="6811-42dc-4454-3dcc" hidden="false">
              <description>Van Wyk may not be your Field Commander.</description>
            </rule>
